Zig syntax notes:
- Every statement ends with semicolon, including `return x;`.
- `if`, `while`, `switch` conditions need parentheses: `if (!done)`, never `if !done`.
- String escapes: only `\n \r \t \\ \' \" \xNN`; no `\v` or `\f`. We don't need escapes.
- Check stdlib names: `std.ascii.isWhitespace`, etc. We might use `std.mem.eql`.
- Copy exact function names and signatures.
- Loops: `for (items) |item| { ... }`, `for (items, 0..) |item, i|`, `while (cond) : (i += 1)`. No C-style `for (;;)`.
- Strings are `[]const u8`; iterate bytes with `for (s) |c|`. Build strings with allocator, not `+`. We use buffer.
- Casts explicit: `@intCast(x)`, `@floatFromInt(x)`, `@as(u32, @intCast(x))`. Integer types never convert implicitly.
- Shift amounts must be u5/u6-sized type or comptime-known: use `@intCast` on RHS of `<<` and `>>`.
- `var` locals that are never mutated are a compile error; use `const`.
- No exceptions and no null unless optional.
- Prefer stdlib helpers.

